diff --git a/.claude/agents/lessons/audit-verifier.md b/.claude/agents/lessons/audit-verifier.md
index 770f28bb..a81dd613 100644
--- a/.claude/agents/lessons/audit-verifier.md
+++ b/.claude/agents/lessons/audit-verifier.md
@@ -5,3 +5,5 @@
 - (2026-10-03, #19) A verifier's own counts need measuring too: the previous verification wrote "22 drafts" and "code 1-11 (9 drafts)" from memory of the manifest; counting the files and the `title:` lines gave 23 drafts. Count with a command before writing a number. (Count drafts, findings and lines with a command before writing any number in the verdict.)
 - (2026-10-03, #21) An empty-diff issue ("created in error", delivered under a successor) went through all stages cleanly. The verifier can finish by re-running the successor's filtered unit, guard and contract tests and comparing the per-file union of hits to tests.md, which takes about 3 minutes once built. (For an empty-diff audit, re-run the tests stage's filtered runs and compare per-file figures; that is enough to verify it.)
 - (2026-10-03, #22) Both corrections from the previous FAIL (a draft built from a "- none" Findings section plus trailing prose, and a duration written from memory) were fixed by re-running only the named stages. The re-verification could stay narrow: recompute the duration from the timestamps, list the draft directory in both the worktree and the main checkout, and count the numbered findings with a command. (After a FAIL, re-verify narrowly: recompute figures from their source, list the draft directory in the worktree and the main checkout, count numbered findings with a command.)
+- (2026-10-03, #25) For an empty-diff closed-in-error audit, the whole filtered run (unit, guard, contract, integration with Docker) takes about 3 minutes in total once built. Re-running it and parsing cobertura by leaf file name reproduced tests.md exactly. Key the union by file leaf name plus line number, because a path-keyed union double-counts files that appear under different class paths. (When re-computing coverage unions from several cobertura files, key lines by file leaf name plus line number; a full-path key double-counts files that appear under different class paths.)
+- (2026-10-03, #27) Re-read the drafts' prose after every remediation regeneration, not only the file names and headers: the second pass found a new false claim in a regenerated draft. (After every remediation regeneration re-read each draft's prose claims (Description, Root Cause, Proposed Fix), not only names, headers and labels.)
diff --git a/.claude/agents/lessons/docs-reviewer.md b/.claude/agents/lessons/docs-reviewer.md
index d4cd792c..0d6e9cb6 100644
--- a/.claude/agents/lessons/docs-reviewer.md
+++ b/.claude/agents/lessons/docs-reviewer.md
@@ -21,3 +21,7 @@
 - (2026-10-03, #21) When the code stage ends on an empty diff (issue closed in error, delivery under a successor), the docs stage can end with one search for the proposed-but-absent identifiers across all `*.md` files, plus a check that no page documents them. It does not need to review the successor's pages. (For a closed-in-error issue with an empty diff, search all *.md for the proposed-but-absent identifiers and stop; the successor's pages belong to its own audit.)
 - (2026-10-03, #21) Docs stage: it said `cursor-pagination.md`, `crypto-shredding.md` and `audit-marten.md` "only mention the word" projection. `data-retention.md` also does. This did not change any outcome. Docs stages should list matches from the search output, not from memory. (List search matches from the command output, never from memory.)
 - (2026-10-03, #23) The docs stage cites `EncinaFixture.cs:37`; the class declaration is at `src/Encina.Testing/EncinaFixture.cs:42` (docs stage wrong by five lines; the draft uses :42). (Read every cited line (and the file's line count) before writing a file:line citation (audit #23 FAIL: ROADMAP.md:3102 in an 841-line file, EncinaFixture.cs:37 for :42).)
+- (2026-10-03, #26) The `artifacts/` tree is ignored by ripgrep, so Grep never sees the audit's own artifacts; docs-stage claims about hits inside `artifacts/` must be verified with `Select-String`, and a docs stage that counts "N files" should say whether its own artifact is included. (In audit mode, search with `Select-String` (PowerShell) when a claim covers `artifacts/`, because Grep/ripgrep ignores that tree; when counting matching files, say whether the audit's own artifacts are included.)
+- (2026-10-03, #27) A closed-in-error issue whose feature was later rejected by an ADR needs a decision check as well as an absence check: the ADR rejecting the feature (here ADR-005) and the open backlog issue (#50) contradict each other, and only the docs stage reading the ADR index sees it. (For a proposed-but-absent feature, also check docs/architecture/adr/index.md for an ADR that rejects or defers it and compare its status with the open backlog issue; a rejection contradicted by an open plan, with no superseding ADR, is a finding.)
+- (2026-10-03, #27) A roadmap sentence that mixes ✅-marked and unmarked items under a "completed" heading reads as delivered for the unmarked ones; search roadmap sections by heading, not only by identifier. (In ROADMAP.md check items by their section heading as well as by issue number: an unmarked item inside a "completed" section reads as delivered.)
+- (2026-10-03, #27) Read every cited line number back with `Select-String` (line numbers from a zero-based array index are off by one) and check "elsewhere the page says X" claims with a search before writing them (audit #27 verifier FAIL: heading at 318 not 317, lead-in at 320 not 319, and ROADMAP.md mentions #50/#51 only at line 324). (Cite line numbers only from Select-String's LineNumber (never a zero-based array index), and run a search before writing "the page elsewhere says X".)
diff --git a/.claude/agents/lessons/issue-archivist.md b/.claude/agents/lessons/issue-archivist.md
index 79d0bb7e..81f96d84 100644
--- a/.claude/agents/lessons/issue-archivist.md
+++ b/.claude/agents/lessons/issue-archivist.md
@@ -17,3 +17,5 @@
 - (2026-10-03, #22) The checker requires block-style empty lists (`prs:` with nothing after), not `[]`, and rejects `current: yes` without a non-`none` destination, so a historical-only entry must use `current: no`. (Empty lists are block style (`prs:` with nothing after); a historical-only knowledge entry uses `current: no` (the validator rejects `current: yes` without a real destination).)
 - (2026-10-03, #24) Compute every duration from the gh timestamps and write both timestamps in the record: the record said "eleven minutes" but created_at 2025-12-24T11:32:02Z and closed_at 11:52:27Z are 20 minutes 25 seconds apart (third audit in a row with a wrong duration). (Compute every duration from gh createdAt/closedAt and write both timestamps; never state a duration from memory (wrong in audits #22, #23 and #24).)
 - (2026-10-03, #24) A pre-draft lists packages straight from an unticked template checklist (here `Encina.Caching.*`, `Encina.AspNetCore` etc. were all unchecked); take packages from the code that shipped, not from the template. (Take the record's packages from the code that shipped, never from an unticked template checklist in the issue or the pre-draft.)
+- (2026-10-03, #25) The record validator requires `audit`, block-list (not `[]`) fields, and a non-`none` destination for `current: yes`; a duplicate record can use `docs` -> CHANGELOG.md as the destination. (Before writing a record, check it against knowledge-records.cs rules: `audit` present, block-list fields (never `[]`), and a non-`none` destination when `current: yes` (a duplicate can point `docs` at CHANGELOG.md).)
+- (2026-10-03, #26) An issue closed "created in error" is a duplicate of its same-scope re-creation (#42 here, #52 for audit #25): compare bodies, then record `outcome: duplicate` with `duplicate_of`, rather than `rejected-unexplained`. I first chose rejected-unexplained; state_reason COMPLETED and a different title ("enhancements" vs "enhanced DLQ handling") hid the match. (An issue closed "created in error" is a duplicate of its same-scope re-creation even when the title differs: search same-scope issues created soon after, compare bodies, and record `outcome: duplicate` with `duplicate_of` (audits #25 -> #52, #26 -> #42); never settle on rejected-unexplained before that search.)
diff --git a/.claude/agents/lessons/issue-auditor.md b/.claude/agents/lessons/issue-auditor.md
index 5229568c..9135ea11 100644
--- a/.claude/agents/lessons/issue-auditor.md
+++ b/.claude/agents/lessons/issue-auditor.md
@@ -14,3 +14,4 @@
 - (2026-10-03, #19) code stage (code 9): missed `docs/ci-cd-templates.md`, which documents the `coverage-threshold` input and recommends values (`:49`, `:87`, `:111`, `:132`, `:207`, `:255`, `:293`); the code 9 draft covers it. (When a finding names an input, option or flag, search docs/ for it too, so the pages that document it are in the finding.)
 - (2026-10-03, #19) code stage (code 8): did not notice that `.github/scripts/coverage-weights.json` points `$schema` at a `coverage-weights-schema.json` that does not exist. (For a JSON or config file in a finding, check that its $schema and other references resolve.)
 - (2026-10-03, #21) When the archivist reports that an issue was closed in error and delivered no code, the code stage can end at confirming the empty diff and the existence or absence of the proposed types, with "- none" findings. Walking out to the successor's code would duplicate that successor's audit. (For a closed-in-error issue with an empty diff, confirm the empty diff and the proposed types, report "- none", and leave the successor's code to the successor's own audit.)
+- (2026-10-03, #27) Negative search claims in stage text must quote the exact pattern and be run in the worktree; two were broader than the search supported in this audit. (A negative search claim states the exact pattern, file types and folders searched, run in the audit worktree, and never generalises beyond them (audit #27: "no *Generator* directory" and "no Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.CSharp match" were both false).)
diff --git a/.claude/agents/lessons/remediation-drafter.md b/.claude/agents/lessons/remediation-drafter.md
index d01dd477..75b0e7af 100644
--- a/.claude/agents/lessons/remediation-drafter.md
+++ b/.claude/agents/lessons/remediation-drafter.md
@@ -1,3 +1,4 @@
 # Lessons for remediation-drafter
 
 No lessons yet.
+- (2026-10-03, #27) A Root Cause sentence that asserts an ordering ("X was planned before Y was written") needs both dates checked with `git log` or the issue and ADR dates before it goes into a draft. (Never assert an order of events in Root Cause without both dates verified (file date line, issue createdAt in the stage files); if a date cannot be verified, drop the ordering claim.)
diff --git a/.claude/agents/lessons/test-auditor.md b/.claude/agents/lessons/test-auditor.md
index e65fafca..caee2877 100644
--- a/.claude/agents/lessons/test-auditor.md
+++ b/.claude/agents/lessons/test-auditor.md
@@ -26,3 +26,9 @@
 - (2026-10-03, #22) A `## Findings` section with no findings contains only `- none`. Any prose after it, even an explanation that the gaps are informational, is parsed by the remediation drafter as a finding. Put informational gaps in a separate section such as `## Informational (not findings)`. (A Findings section with no findings contains only "- none"; informational gaps go in a separate "## Informational (not findings)" section (audit #22 FAIL).)
 - (2026-10-03, #23) A filter `FullyQualifiedName~EncinaFixtureTests` does not match `EncinaTestFixtureTests`; a class-name filter must be checked against the class list, and the Base\ duplicate folder makes every such filter run both copies. (Check a class-name test filter against the actual class list before running it; tests/Encina.UnitTests/Testing/Base duplicates Testing/ (#1693), so filters there run both copies.)
 - (2026-10-03, #24) For a closed-in-error issue with an empty diff, the archivist's "tests not located by file name" note is the one useful input: a `Select-String -List` over `tests\` for the successor's class names answers it in one call, and a narrow filtered run of the successor's namespaces confirms the tests pass; per-file gaps go to the successor's audit (#35), not to the empty issue. (Locate a successor's tests with one Select-String -List over tests\ for its class names before the filtered run.)
+- (2026-10-03, #25) For a closed-in-error issue whose duplicate delivered the code, the one-call `Select-String -List` over `tests\` for the duplicate's class names (lesson of #24) located 13 test files at once; a narrow filtered run of all four flags under Release was quick enough (the integration run itself reported 916 ms with Docker available), so run integration whenever Docker is up. (When Docker is up, run the integration flag too: a filtered integration run of a small feature takes about a second once built, so skipping it is never justified by time.)
+- (2026-10-03, #25) The filtered contract run needs the bare namespace (`Encina.ContractTests.Marten`) while the guard tests of the same feature live in two namespaces (`...Marten.Snapshots` and `...Infrastructure.Marten`); a name-based filter (`Snapshot&Marten`) caught both, a namespace-suffix filter would have dropped one. (Filter test runs by feature name (`FullyQualifiedName~Snapshot&FullyQualifiedName~Marten`) rather than by a namespace suffix: one feature's tests can live in several namespaces per flag.)
+- (2026-10-03, #25) stage tests: '- none' followed by prose; prose ignored (Under `## Findings` write the `- none` marker alone; any explanation goes under `## Informational (not findings)` (prose after the marker is ignored and recorded as a pipeline lesson since #1694).)
+- (2026-10-03, #25) A "the only references are" claim should come from a Grep over `tests\` for the symbol, not from the reflection tests alone. Mock set-ups also reference the method without executing the implementation, so say "no test executes it" and cite the measured zero lines. (Never claim "the only references are" from memory or from one test kind: Grep `tests\` for the symbol, and when the point is that nothing executes it, say "no test executes it" and cite the measured zero lines (mock set-ups reference a method without running it).)
+- (2026-10-03, #26) A `FullyQualifiedName~DeadLetter` filter matches the CDC dead-letter contract and property tests too (`Cdc\ICdcDeadLetterStoreContractTests.cs`, `Cdc\InMemoryCdcDeadLetterStorePropertyTests.cs`): a green contract or property count from a name filter does not mean the feature has contract or property tests. State which test files the passing tests belong to, and read the per-file lines executed. (A green count from a name filter is not evidence the feature has tests of that flag: list the test files the passing tests belong to and read the per-file lines executed (a `~DeadLetter` filter also matched the CDC dead-letter tests).)
+- (2026-10-03, #27) For a closed-in-error issue with an empty diff and an open successor (#27 to #50), the whole test stage is one `Select-String` over `tests\` for the proposed symbols plus a manifest search; no test run is needed because nothing in the scope can be executed. Run a filtered successor-test run only when the successor already delivered code (as in #24 and #25). (For a closed-in-error issue with an empty diff: if the successor is still open, the stage is one Select-String over tests\ for the proposed symbols plus a manifest search (no test run); run the successor's tests only when it already delivered code.)
